Shoalcade: cheats through retro_cheat_set / retro_cheat_reset for the PCEE2 libretro core (PS2), as Shoalcade's
LRPS2 patch (tools/lrps2-patches/0003). Upstream's were empty. A code is one or more lines joined by '+' (or new
lines); each line is a pnach line ("patch=1,EE,2XXXXXXX,extended,YYYYYYYY") or a raw decrypted code
("XXXXXXXX YYYYYYYY", turned into patch=1,EE,XXXXXXXX,extended,YYYYYYYY: applied every vsync). A code with an
unreadable line is skipped whole (logged). Encrypted codes (CodeBreaker, GameShark, Action Replay MAX) are not
read. The codes form their own always-enabled patch group (not tied to the "enable cheats" option, which is about
pnach files), rebuilt on the CPU thread and kept across patch reloads and boots. Nothing is written to the cheats
folder, the memory cards or the system folder.

